WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.118
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:09.257
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.557 --> 00:00:15.913
Unit thirteen: Phrasal Verbs (common). Today you will use common phrasal verbs with the right grammar.

4
00:00:16.213 --> 00:00:19.005
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:23.095
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:24.835
Give up.

7
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.652
Give up means to stop trying.

8
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.460
Never give up.

9
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.400
Your turn. Say: Give up.

10
00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:35.966
Give up.

11
00:00:36.717 --> 00:00:37.787
Look after.

12
00:00:38.783 --> 00:00:40.841
Look after means to take care of.

13
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:43.124
I look after my sister.

14
00:00:43.717 --> 00:00:46.299
Your turn. Say: Look after.

15
00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:50.169
Look after.

16
00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:51.581
Turn off.

17
00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:55.070
Turn off means to stop a machine or light.

18
00:00:55.683 --> 00:00:56.893
Turn off the TV.

19
00:00:57.483 --> 00:01:00.287
Your turn. Say: Turn off.

20
00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:03.949
Turn off.

21
00:01:04.683 --> 00:01:05.475
Put off.

22
00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:08.378
Put off means to delay something.

23
00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:10.344
Don't put off the work.

24
00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.347
Your turn. Say: Put off.

25
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.108
Put off.

26
00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.037
Separable.

27
00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:22.746
Separable means can be split by an object.

28
00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:24.897
Turn it off is separable.

29
00:01:25.483 --> 00:01:27.857
Your turn. Say: Separable.

30
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.736
Separable.

31
00:01:32.483 --> 00:01:33.682
Inseparable.

32
00:01:34.683 --> 00:01:36.869
Inseparable means cannot be split.

33
00:01:37.483 --> 00:01:39.320
Look after is inseparable.

34
00:01:39.917 --> 00:01:42.581
Your turn. Say: Inseparable.

35
00:01:45.433 --> 00:01:46.551
Inseparable.

36
00:01:47.317 --> 00:01:48.225
Particle.

37
00:01:49.217 --> 00:01:52.041
Particle means the small word in a phrasal verb.

38
00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.046
Up is a particle.

39
00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:56.850
Your turn. Say: Particle.

40
00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:00.631
Particle.

41
00:02:01.383 --> 00:02:02.210
Meaning.

42
00:02:03.217 --> 00:02:05.750
Meaning means what a word or phrase says.

43
00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.699
The meaning changes.

44
00:02:08.283 --> 00:02:10.611
Your turn. Say: Meaning.

45
00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:14.247
Meaning.

46
00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:18.336
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:19.183 --> 00:02:22.274
Visal, use two common phrasal verbs in a sentence.

48
00:02:23.383 --> 00:02:34.955
I look after my sister, and I never give up. A phrasal verb is a verb plus a particle such as up, off or after. The meaning is often different from the single words.

49
00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.794
Can I put an object in the middle?

50
00:02:38.883 --> 00:02:52.419
With separable verbs, yes: Turn the light off. Turn it off. A pronoun object must go in the middle. With inseparable verbs, no: I look after her, not look her after.

51
00:02:53.517 --> 00:02:54.564
How do I learn them?

52
00:02:55.650 --> 00:03:08.150
In groups and sentences. Give up means stop, put off means delay, and look after means care for. Many phrasal verbs have more than one meaning, so check a dictionary.

53
00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.824
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.683 --> 00:03:15.540
Grammar focus: Phrasal verbs: separable and inseparable.

55
00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.051
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.610
I look after my little sister.

57
00:03:20.517 --> 00:03:21.878
Please turn it off.

58
00:03:22.783 --> 00:03:23.854
Don't give up!

59
00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:34.688
A phrasal verb = verb + particle. With separable verbs, a pronoun object goes in the middle (turn it off). Inseparable verbs cannot be split (look after her).

60
00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:38.938
Be careful! Don't say: Please turn off it.

61
00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.807
Say: Please turn it off.

62
00:03:43.107 --> 00:03:44.584
Put a pronoun in the middle.

63
00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.238
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.534
Verbs with Particles.

65
00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:53.634
I look after my little sister when my parents work.

66
00:03:54.633 --> 00:03:57.306
Please turn off the TV and don't put off your homework.

67
00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.265
If it is difficult, never give up.

68
00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:04.741
Some phrasal verbs are separable, but others are inseparable.

69
00:04:05.733 --> 00:04:08.604
The meaning of a phrasal verb is often not obvious.

70
00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:13.864
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:14.717 --> 00:04:17.148
Please blank the light. (stop it)

72
00:04:17.448 --> 00:04:21.439
A, turn off. B, look after. C, give in.

73
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.814
The answer is A: turn off.

74
00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.404
She blank her little brother.

75
00:04:29.704 --> 00:04:33.706
A, looks after. B, looks him after. C, after looks.

76
00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:39.278
The answer is A: looks after.

77
00:04:40.417 --> 00:04:41.917
Which sentence is correct?

78
00:04:42.217 --> 00:04:46.428
A, Turn off it.. B, Turn it off.. C, Turn off it please..

79
00:04:49.967 --> 00:04:51.931
The answer is B: Turn it off..

80
00:04:53.083 --> 00:04:54.479
'Put off' means blank.

81
00:04:54.779 --> 00:04:58.584
A, delay. B, wear. C, start.

82
00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:03.819
The answer is A: delay.

83
00:05:04.983 --> 00:05:07.494
According to the reading, what should you never do?

84
00:05:07.794 --> 00:05:11.610
A, give up. B, turn off. C, look after.

85
00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:17.039
The answer is A: give up.

86
00:05:18.233 --> 00:05:21.211
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:25.025
Write two sentences using common phrasal verbs.

88
00:05:33.817 --> 00:05:35.387
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:35.687 --> 00:05:48.022
I always look after my younger brother, and I never give up when my homework is difficult. In these sentences, look after and give up are phrasal verbs, and each one has a special meaning.

90
00:05:48.322 --> 00:05:50.008
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:56.483
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and phrasal verbs: separable and inseparable.

92
00:05:56.783 --> 00:06:01.270
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

93
00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:04.315
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:04.615 --> 00:06:08.057
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

